# Bitwise, over whole numbers 64 bits wide.
#
# Conjunction and disjunction are the spaced operators `&` and `|`, which is
# also how a reader spells them. What is named here is what no operator says.
#
# A shift moves by 0 to 63 places. Anything else is undefined in the machine
# and answers differently by host, so it is refused rather than guessed at.
# Shifting right keeps the sign, which is what go, rust and java all spell
# `>>`.
pub fn not a
  builtin_bit_not a

pub fn shl a places
  builtin_bit_shl a places

pub fn shr a places
  builtin_bit_shr a places

pub fn xor a b
  builtin_bit_xor a b
